INTERPRETATION

The LU-2R Task-3 learned-U transfer has now repeated on a second completely
fresh world set.

The frozen learned recruiter again controlled only 25 percent of U
recruitment probability and remained blind to task, program, stage, phase,
lesion, global queue, evaluator correctness, absolute position, and future
information.

It caused 63 real developmental recruitment changes in the fair-world subset
while every qualified pair preserved throughput, backlog, cost, streams,
repair, recovery, correctness, and matching integrity.

This independently confirms that the learned local recruitment behavior
generalizes into the deeper three-stage task rather than reflecting a lucky
LU-2R world set.

BOUNDARY

Do not increase alpha.

Do not give learned authority to C/S.

Do not add online adaptation or recursive self-modification.

NEXT SCIENTIFIC QUESTION

Increase task distance again while returning first to exact-parent
environment validation.

The smallest clean next step is a four-stage compositional transform task at
the same one-request-per-epoch external load and inherited perturbation
regime.

Validate exact-parent feasibility before reintroducing U_A25.

PLAIN-SPEAK INTERPRETATION

The three-step result repeated.

On ten new worlds, the neural recruiter again made real cell-development
decisions while the organism stayed inside the hand-written parent's envelope
in every fair comparison.

No wrong answers.
No expired jobs.
No authority increase.

That makes the Task-3 transfer substantially harder to explain as chance.

The next useful move is a deeper four-step job, starting with the
hand-written parent alone so we know the new environment is fair before the
neural recruiter gets tested there.

